# What this repository had to invent. The absence census over the documents that stipulate a
# state rather than attest to one.
#
# States no real filing produced
#   Every row is a state no real filing produced. A fixture exists because the corpus never reached
#   the combination it asserts, so this relation is the list of branches the model can handle and
#   has never actually met in the wild. That is a different and more uncomfortable reading of the
#   same census.
#
# Nothing here may be counted as evidence
#   These are stipulations. They prove the code path works and say nothing whatever about the
#   world.
-- reports/absence_census.sqlc at fixture scope.
:compose(reports/absence_census.sqlc, @scope = scope/fixtures.sqlc)
